ECHO - DISPLAY COMMAND-LINE TEXT

CALLER. Subject to the current caller access policy.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
ECHO - DISPLAY COMMAND-LINE TEXT

CALLER. Subject to the current caller access policy.

Syntax:
    ECHO text

Writes the supplied text to the console. Example: ECHO HELLO

Useful in aliases and command sequences. It does not save a message or
contact the sysop. Use MESSAGE for a stored note and CHAT for a page.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
